---
permalink: "/review/index.html"
layout: base.njk
pageTitle: "Landing pages for review | LIMRA Overseas Education"
pageDescription: "Index of the six LIMRA campus landing pages, for review before the advertising campaign goes live."
---

{#- An unlisted index, for sending to the client so they can click through all
    six in one sitting. Nothing links here, so the bare domain stays a plain
    holding page and the campus pages keep their no-navigation design, which is
    the reason they convert. Carries the same noindex as every other page. -#}

<section class="lp-review">
  <div class="lp-review-inner">

    <p class="lp-eyebrow lp-eyebrow--dark">For review</p>
    <h1>The six campus landing pages</h1>
    <p class="lp-ty-lead">One page per partner university, each built to turn an advertising click into an enquiry. Every link on this page opens in a new tab, so this index stays put while you look through them.</p>

    <div class="lp-404-grid">
      {%- for c in campuses %}
      <a href="/{{ c.id }}/" class="lp-404-card" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
        <img src="/assets/campus/{{ c.id }}-logo.webp" alt="" loading="lazy" />
        <span>
          <strong>{{ c.shortName | safe }}</strong>
          <em>{{ c.city }}, {{ c.country }}</em>
        </span>
      </a>
      {%- endfor %}
    </div>

    <div class="lp-review-note">
      <h2>What to look at</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Try it on a phone as well as a computer. Most advertising traffic arrives on mobile.</li>
        <li>Start filling the enquiry form and watch the page dim around it.</li>
        <li>Tap a campus photograph to open it larger.</li>
        <li>Move your cursor towards the top of the browser window as though leaving.</li>
      </ul>

      <p class="lp-review-warn">
        <strong>Please do not submit a real test enquiry without telling the team.</strong>
        The form is live, so a test arrives in the same inbox as genuine student
        enquiries. If you do want to test it, use a name like "TEST, please ignore".
      </p>

      <h2>Supporting pages</h2>
      <ul class="lp-review-links">
        <li><a href="/privacy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Privacy policy</a>, required by Google Ads and linked from every form</li>
        <li><a href="/404.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Not-found page</a>, shown if anyone mistypes an address</li>
        <li><a href="/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Holding page</a>, what the bare domain shows</li>
      </ul>

      <p class="lp-review-fine">
        This index is not linked from anywhere and is hidden from search engines,
        along with the campus pages themselves. The campus pages carry no
        navigation on purpose: the only ways onward are the form, a phone call,
        or WhatsApp.
      </p>
    </div>

  </div>
</section>
